From 9ee3f293025a9f701b8e996c89d7e07a76b35a2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kobbler-Media <dev@kobbler.invalid>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:20:46 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] server: LLAMA_WORKER_ISOLATION parent/child split + lifecycle
 endpoints

Re-graft of 177a650ae onto upstream 8fc037672 (server.cpp is now split into
roles, so the parent is its own role, server_run_worker_parent, dispatched
before any device enumeration).

A CUDA-free parent owns the port and runs the model in a child process on a
private port, proxying every model-facing route to it. Killing the child is
the only way to return ALL of its VRAM (the CUDA primary context lives until
the process exits), which kob-gpu-gate needs to lend the card to other jobs.

  POST /v1/admin/drain   503 new model requests; in-flight ones finish
  POST /v1/admin/unload  SIGKILL the child (also /admin/unload)
  POST /unload           same; the path kob-gpu-gate uses for light services
  POST /v1/admin/load    spawn the child and clear drain
  GET  /health           {status, model, loaded, busy, draining, in_flight}
  GET  /v1/gpu/status    {loaded, gpu, busy}, only with WORKER_GPU_STATUS=1
                         (the always-resident LLM is booked by a standing
                         reservation; answering here would change that)

WORKER_LOAD_ON_START=1 spawns the child at boot (always-on services; after an
/unload it returns lazily on the next model request). WORKER_DEFAULT_GPU picks the child's card, the X-Worker-Gpu header relocates
it per request, and WORKER_IDLE_UNLOAD_SECONDS unloads it after that long
idle. A request counts as in flight from arrival, so the idle reaper cannot
take the child down between spawn and forward.

Validated on the 5060 Ti with EmbeddingGemma-2: parent alone holds no VRAM,
a metadata poll does not spawn, /unload returns the card to baseline, reload
1.0 s, drain 503s, idle reaper fires, /v1/gpu/status reports the UUID.
